obilize, distract, polarize, or dehumanize."}, {"id": "f1f83f34-a4e5-4fc8-832d-a347a22e6e39", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Misinformation dynamics", "children": [{"id": "52e158b6-7bbc-4ff7-919e-9d46da65bed9", "type": "concept", "title": "rumors"}, {"id": "df23425c-2474-4ca9-aab5-f09db2896779", "type": "concept", "title": "conspiracy narratives"}, {"id": "12f6c223-b7af-47d9-8158-4e445a8c849a", "type": "concept", "title": "virality"}, {"id": "20632f51-4c9b-4fa7-aa37-1369c8488f44", "type": "concept", "title": "correction limits"}], "description": "Why it matters: False or misleading claims spread through social, emotional, and platform incentives."}, {"id": "f3e25606-42a4-49ce-90c8-5c971e27beb9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Counter-propaganda and resilience", "children": [{"id": "bf0fb3ac-372a-467d-9fa7-ce271566de57", "type": "concept", "title": "prebunking"}, {"id": "dc1aaf3a-9fa2-4f5d-8679-ebebcaa376bb", "type": "concept", "title": "source tracing"}, {"id": "e15c456b-7730-474b-9f9b-04109ba9842d", "type": "concept", "title": "media literacy"}, {"id": "4e25db51-ca1a-48be-9f1d-b63d2d84a944", "type": "concept", "title": "community trust"}], "description": "Why it matters: Students learn responses that strengthen judgment without amplifying harm."}]}, {"id": "e4f9d290-9d32-445c-bb33-0c88c2006c56", "type": "topic", "title": "Advertising, Branding, and Consumer Persuasion", "description": "Advertising applies persuasion to markets, identity, desire, and attention. Students analyze how brands create meaning and influence choice.", "children": [{"id": "067ba957-42be-4918-b9f4-96dded1eda69", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Advertising appeals", "children": [{"id": "f4f12bb8-5307-43fd-ad08-e90e9698a34b", "type": "concept", "title": "fear appeals"}, {"id": "11e6fbf3-0a1b-41bf-9cbd-9742a3715012", "type": "concept", "title": "humor"}, {"id": "63c61953-14ab-4de9-b9a3-0938904a56ba", "type": "concept", "title": "aspiration"}, {"id": "a194f326-ee7f-4774-a827-e79ab23854ad", "type": "c